{# Accordion — schema.org FAQPage structured data (opt-in per block).

   Emitted only when the editor ticks "faqSchema", because the markup asserts
   that the block IS a list of frequently asked questions; using it on a generic
   accordion would misdescribe the page.

   Answers keep the plain HTML schema.org accepts in an answer (headings,
   paragraphs, lists, emphasis) and lose every other tag. That includes the
   `<sulu-link>` tags the text editor stores for an internal link, whose text
   stays. They must not reach the JSON: json_encode escapes the closing tag as
   `<\/sulu-link>`, and Sulu's markup parser, which rewrites these tags across
   the whole response, then counts a tag it can never extract and calls itself
   again until the request times out.

   json_encode escapes quotes, backslashes and control characters, and - with
   default flags - forward slashes too, so a `</script>` inside the content
   comes out as `<\/script>` and cannot close the tag early. Keep the default
   flags. `|raw` is required because Twig's HTML autoescaping would turn the
   JSON quotes into entities and break the document.

   Expected variables:
     - items: the repeatable block items (itemTitle, itemContent)
#}
{% set questions = [] %}
{% for item in items %}
    {% if item.type|default('item') == 'item' and item.itemTitle|default('') is not empty and item.itemContent|default('') is not empty %}
        {% set questions = questions|merge([{
            '@type': 'Question',
            'name': item.itemTitle,
            'acceptedAnswer': {
                '@type': 'Answer',
                'text': item.itemContent|striptags('<h1><h2><h3><h4><h5><h6><p><br><ul><ol><li><strong><b><em><i>')
            }
        }]) %}
    {% endif %}
{% endfor %}

{% if questions is not empty %}
    <script type="application/ld+json">{{ {
        '@context': 'https://schema.org',
        '@type': 'FAQPage',
        'mainEntity': questions
    }|json_encode|raw }}</script>
{% endif %}
